course: dictionary
lesson: 3294
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning is needed. The word estate is a good example. «An estate agent helps sell houses, and viewings are when people who might buy come to look round.» An estate agent helps people buy and sell houses, so estate here is linked to homes.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. In «Royal and noble women ran estates, managed money and wrote letters», the clues managed money and ran suggest a large area of land with a big house, owned and looked after by a family.
explain: A housing estate is a different kind of estate. «In Oxford, Barnaby finds out his friend from the estate gets free school meals» tells you the friend lives there, so the estate is an area with many houses or flats built together. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: An estate is a large area of land in the country, often with a big house, owned by one person or family.
fact: A housing estate is an area with many houses or flats built together, like the one Barnaby's friend lives on.
fact: A person's estate is all the money and things they own, especially what is left when they die.
fact: An estate car is a car with a long back for luggage.
fact: Real estate (in the US) is land and buildings that are bought and sold, and an estate agent helps with this.
exercise: «An estate agent helps sell houses, and viewings are when people who might buy come to look round.» What is an estate agent's job? | Growing crops on a farm | Driving long-distance buses | *Helping people buy and sell houses
exercise: «Royal and noble women ran estates, managed money and wrote letters.» In this sentence, what is an estate? | *A large area of land with a big house, owned by a family | A car with a long back for luggage | A small garden for growing flowers
exercise: «In Oxford, Barnaby finds out his friend from the estate gets free school meals.» What is the estate in this sentence? | A bag of money | A car for carrying luggage | A big house in the country with gardens | *A place with many houses or flats built together
test: Which phrase means a car with a long back for luggage? | estate agent | real estate | *estate car | housing estate
test: What is a person's estate? | The house they live in, and nothing else | The cars they have never sold | A map of the countryside | *All the money and things they own, especially what is left when they die
exam: Read «An estate agent helps sell a house; a survey checks it for problems; a mortgage from the bank pays for most of it.» What does a survey do? | *Checks a house for problems | Helps people move into a new country | Sells cars to families | Pays for most of the house
